{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122598-question-about-how-humanity-morality-works-first-edition","id":1122598,"title":"Question about how Humanity/Morality works (First Edition)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-29T21:12:14-07:00","id":1122598,"title":"Question about how Humanity/Morality works (First Edition)","content":"I ALWAYS had complications when understanding this system...So...Killing is fine unless is justified? and what do i have to roll not to go lower in the scale of humanity.<br /> also, lets say that my character has humanity 7..he decided to Cannibalize a woman infront of her husband and feed him the remains. Other than being mentally fucked up..and considering thats lower on the humanity scale (a 4, to give an example) would i have to roll to go One level lower or would i jump from 7 down to 4.<br /> <br /> please explain me as if i was an idiot..then again, i am an idiot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T21:22:16-07:00","id":1122601,"title":"","content":"I believe a failed Morality roll drops you down a single dot. So if you're at Morality 7 and commit a crime against Morality 4, then fail the roll to resist degradation, you dip down to 6.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T21:34:15-07:00","id":1122606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122598-question-about-how-humanity-morality-works-first-edition#post1122598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ALWAYS had complications when understanding this system...So...Killing is fine unless is justified?</div> </div> </div> </div>Killing is worse for your ability to relate to other people if you do it with greater frequency or deliberation. A person who kills somebody else in the heat of the moment or through gross negligence is more sympathetic to the average person on the street than someone who stalks the back alleys looking for redheaded children to kill or someone who meticulously plotted the deaths of fourteen people. The 1e Morality track is more about how disconnected you are from common mores and taboos than Integrity's focus on self-image and worldview.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> also, lets say that my character has humanity 7..he decided to Cannibalize a woman infront of her husband and feed him the remains. Other than being mentally fucked up..and considering thats lower on the humanity scale (a 4, to give an example) would i have to roll to go One level lower or would i jump from 7 down to 4. </div> </div> </div>Next level down and you have a fairly direct justification for penalizing the derangement roll and skipping directly to a severe derangement. Respecting the fiction means understanding that characters with Humanity 7 aren't generally at the place where brutal acts of gore-display are at the forefront of their minds as things to actually do.<br /> <br /> This behavior doesn't come from nowhere in-setting and the Trait doesn't exist as an in-universe metric that characters know about, so a character that had an followed through on an inexplicable impulse to force-feed a man his wife's flesh once is going to be in a different place than a character who has embraced that impulse as a regular part of their life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T22:09:05-07:00","id":1122612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1122598-question-about-how-humanity-morality-works-first-edition#post1122598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what do i have to roll not to go lower in the scale of humanity.<br /> also, lets say that my character has humanity 7..he decided to Cannibalize a woman infront of her husband and feed him the remains. Other than being mentally fucked up..and considering thats lower on the humanity scale (a 4, to give an example) would i have to roll to go One level lower or would i jump from 7 down to 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are two things that make Morality sins with lower numbers more severe than those at higher numbers. The first is just that they're more consistent: a Morality 3 sin is something almost everybody is shaken by, while a Morality 6 sin is something that doesn't take too long before you're inured to it and don't have to roll for it anymore, because you don't have to roll for any sin at a number higher than your Morality. The second is that you roll fewer dice to resist degeneration. Morality rolls are unlike most of the rolls in the Storytelling System because your dice pool to resist degeneration isn't based on any of your traits: it's a flat number specified by the Morality table, and more importantly, it's a <i>small</i> number, smaller than the dice pools you'll be rolling for actions your character is good at. There's a bigger difference between rolling three dice or four dice than there is between rolling six dice or seven dice.<br /> <br /> Morality almost never changes by more than one dot at a time, though, so that's not what makes those sins mechanically nasty, no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}